WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for staticos-halloween.mp4. The spoken lines were transcribed with whisper.cpp
(base.en model, speech-detection on) and tidied by reading; the cue times follow where
each word starts in the audio and can be a second or two out.

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:03.400
It's that time of year again.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.600
The whole desktop dresses up for Halloween,

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.900
a haunted house, falling leaves and bats,

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:19.000
even a jack-o-lantern cursor.

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:24.300
Countdown ticks away to Saturday night.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.200
Once a day, knock on the pumpkin in the dock

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.500
for a treat, like a brand new wallpaper.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.000
Or a trick: carve your own jack-o-lantern,

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.600
light it up, and make it your wallpaper.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.500
There are three spooky new arcade games,

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:06.200
and a badge if you make it out of the haunted maze.

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:10.400
Static Play has a Halloween shelf,

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:14.100
and Static Forge has Halloween games

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:15.700
you can start in one click.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.000
Dress up your profile picture

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.600
as a witch, a vampire, or a ghost.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.000
Type "boo" on the desktop.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:43.200
Happy Halloween from StaticOS.

00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:44.700
Open it in any browser

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:47.500
at staticos.surge.sh.
